      "title": "The ReAct Loop Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The ReAct Loop Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Agent = LLM + Tools + Loop",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Agent== = {blue:LLM} + {orange:tools} + {purple:loop}",
                "The model **picks** the next action",
                "Code **executes** it; the result goes back into the ==context==",
                "Repeat until a final answer"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The ReAct Cycle",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Thought",
                    "sub": "reason about next step",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Action",
                    "sub": "tool call + arguments",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Observation",
                    "sub": "tool result",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Final answer",
                    "sub": "loop ends",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Plain CoT",
                "ReAct"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Facts from",
                  "prompt only",
                  "real tool observations"
                ],
                [
                  "Fetch data?",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Hallucination",
                  "higher",
                  "==lower=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example: Weather in the capital of France?",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Thought",
                    "note": "need the capital",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Action",
                    "note": "search('capital of France')",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Observation",
                    "note": "Paris",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Action",
                    "note": "get_weather('Paris')",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Final answer",
                    "note": "weather in Paris",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "One iteration",
              "text": "Thought → Action → Observation. The loop ends only on a ==final answer=="
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Workflow vs agent?** Workflow: code fixes the steps. Agent: the model picks them.",
                "**Why less hallucination than CoT?** Each step is grounded in real tool observations.",
                "**One loop iteration?** Thought, Action, Observation."
              ],
              "style": "check"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Planning Patterns",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Planning Patterns",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Plan-and-Execute and Re-planning",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Planner} LLM writes the ==full step list== up front",
                "{green:Executor} runs each step in order",
                "Fits ==long, predictable== tasks",
                "==Re-plan== after each step or failure: check plan against observations, then revise",
                "A static plan breaks when a tool result {red:surprises} you"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Plan",
                    "sub": "all steps",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Execute",
                    "sub": "one step",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Check",
                    "sub": "vs observation",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Revise",
                    "sub": "on surprise",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. ReAct vs Plan-and-Execute",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ReAct",
                "Plan-and-execute"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Decides",
                  "**one step** at a time",
                  "**all steps** up front"
                ],
                [
                  "Strength",
                  "flexible",
                  "coherent"
                ],
                [
                  "Weakness",
                  "myopic",
                  "rigid"
                ],
                [
                  "Cost",
                  "more LLM calls",
                  "cheaper"
                ],
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "adaptive tasks",
                  "long, predictable tasks"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Reflection Loop",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Draft",
                    "note": "first output",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Critique",
                    "note": "model judges itself",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Revise",
                    "note": "retry, then repeat",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Cap the rounds",
              "text": "Limit reflection to ==1-3 rounds==. Every round adds LLM calls and latency."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
