          "title": "Multi-Agent Patterns",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three Patterns",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pattern",
                "Shape",
                "Use for"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Orchestrator-worker**",
                  "Lead splits, delegates, merges",
                  "Most common"
                ],
                [
                  "**Pipeline / handoff**",
                  "researcher → writer → reviewer",
                  "Sequential stages"
                ],
                [
                  "**Debate / critic**",
                  "Propose, critique or vote",
                  "Hard, high-stakes answers"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Lead",
                    "sub": "splits task",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Workers",
                    "sub": "specialists",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Lead",
                    "sub": "merges results",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Single vs Multi",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Use multi-agent only if subtasks are {green:parallel}",
                "Or they need ==separate contexts==",
                "Or they need different ==tools or prompts==",
                "Otherwise start with a **single agent**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Cost",
              "text": "Multi-agent ==multiplies token cost== and adds coordination failures."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Single enough?** Yes, unless subtasks are parallel or need separate contexts, tools or prompts",
                "**Sharing context?** Lead sends each worker a task brief; workers return results the lead merges",
                "**Specific failures?** Lost context at handoffs, conflicting outputs, runaway cost, error cascades"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Stopping Conditions, Cost and Latency",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
